	(text_box "NOTES (NTSC build; PAL values in brackets)\nNumbered notes are from Commodore schematic 251138 Rev B; lettered notes are for this\ndesign. Boxed markers show where a note applies.\n\n2. Clock circuit: Y1 = 14.31818 MHz HC-49S (17.734472 MHz). C70 = 16 pF ±5% N2200 (15 pF\nN3300); fitted as C0G because no N2200 part is available, so recheck the colour carrier if\nit drifts while the board warms up. R52 = 680 Ω (330 Ω), R53 = 910 Ω (100 Ω).\n\n8. Dot-clock VCO: C86 = 82 pF ±5% with no R101, for a 6567 rev 8 VIC-II. A 6567 rev 5 or a\nPAL 6569 needs 68 pF plus R101 = 22 kΩ from +Vc to U31 pin 4; R101 has no footprint on the\nPCB.\n\nA. PAL/NTSC jumper: E3 (E1 to E3, jumper_select to GND) selects NTSC and is fitted as a 0 Ω\naxial link. E2 (E1 to E2, jumper_select to +Vc) selects PAL and is not fitted. Never fit\nboth: that shorts +Vc to GND.\n\nB. IC sockets: these chips are not sold by LCSC, so the board gets a round-pin DIP socket\nand the chip is bought separately and inserted after assembly.\nU1: MOS 6526 CIA (CIA 1)\nU2: MOS 6526 CIA (CIA 2)\nU7: MOS 6510 CPU\nU32: Motorola MC4044P phase-frequency detector (obsolete; new-old stock only)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 281.94 15.24 0)
		(size 121.92 48.26)
		(margins 1.27 1.27 1.27 1.27)
		(stroke
			(width 0.254)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "97fbec62-57ee-4ac7-aa6c-f67aec0bf703")
	)
